course: dictionary
lesson: 11094
title: Wheat, from field to bread
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Wheat is a tall grass plant grown on farms. Its grain can be ground into flour, and that flour is used to make bread, pasta and cakes. So the word wheat can mean the plant, and it can also mean the grain itself.
explain: «Before a loaf of bread reaches you, many people work on it: a farmer grows wheat, a miller grinds flour, a baker bakes.» Each person in that line is one step in a chain that starts with a plant. Following the steps from farm to shop shows how food reaches your table.
explain: Machines do a lot of the work now. «A combine harvester cuts the wheat, beats out the grains and blows away the straw at once.» Before machines, this job needed dozens of people with sickles.
fact: Wheat is a cereal crop, which means a plant grown for its grain.
fact: Wheat is grown in big fields in Canada, the USA, Australia and Ukraine.
fact: «Three grains feed much of humanity: rice, wheat and maize.»
fact: «Whole wheat» and «wheat flour» are used in everyday foods, such as wholemeal bread.
fact: «The harvest mouse weaves a ball-shaped nest among tall grass or wheat stalks.» Wheat is a home as well as a crop.
exercise: What is wheat grown for on farms? | Rocks for building | Wool for jumpers | *Grain that is ground into flour | Fish for the market
exercise: «A farmer grows wheat, a miller grinds flour, a baker bakes.» Who grinds the flour? | *A miller | A baker | A farmer | A driver
exercise: Name the three grains that feed much of humanity. | Oak, pine and birch | Carrots, peas and beans | *Rice, wheat and maize | Cows, pigs and sheep
test: «A combine harvester cuts the wheat, beats out the grains and blows away the straw at once.» What does the machine do to the wheat first? | *Cuts it | Bakes it into bread | Sells it in a shop | Turns it into pasta
test: «The harvest mouse weaves a ball-shaped nest among tall grass or wheat stalks.» Where does the harvest mouse build its nest? | Inside a bread oven | *Among tall grass or wheat stalks | In a shop window | Deep under the sea
exam: A pupil writes, «Wheat is a tall grass plant grown on farms.» Which meaning of wheat is this? | The bread | *The plant | The machine that cuts it | The farm shop
